PBE noncollinear LCAO regression for gga_grad=2, including forces and stress.
Derived from scf_angle_spin4; pseudopotential and orbitals reuse tests/PP_ORB.
Uses scalapack_gvx and scf_thr=1e-11 for parallel reference comparisons.

From tests/03_NAO_multik, run:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /path/to/abacus -n 4 -r '^scf_gga_grad2_spin4$'

Generate result.ref with the same command using -n 1 -g. Default energy,
force and stress tolerances apply; no threshold overrides are used.

The reference uses the mapped-density FFT definition of gga_grad=2. A matched
rebuild with the upstream projected-gradient XC reproduces the previous reference;
the mapped definition raises the converged two-atom energy by 0.1075335933 eV
(53.7668 meV/atom) at this deliberately low 15-Ry cutoff. Its absolute-component
stress sum changes from 3941.148224 to 3873.105155 kbar; this sum is a regression
fingerprint, not a stress-component error or an accuracy bound. Both definitions
converge with the unchanged INPUT. One- and four-rank CPU results agree within
the default tolerances, without solver, SCF, or comparison-threshold changes.
This low-cutoff finite-grid difference should not be generalized to converged
cutoffs or interpreted as a uniform energy offset across materials.
